---
const stages = [
	'Kitchen settings',
	'Business and suppliers',
	'Ingredients',
	'Recipes',
	'Menu',
	'First order'
];
---

<section id="setup" class="bg-softgreen" aria-labelledby="setup-heading">
	<div class="container-page py-section-tight">
		<div class="grid items-start gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[5fr_7fr] lg:gap-16">
			<div data-reveal>
				<p class="eyebrow">Guided setup</p>
				<h2 id="setup-heading" class="mt-4 text-h2 font-semibold">From costing settings to a first costed order.</h2>
				<p class="mt-5 max-w-[58ch] text-lede text-ink-soft">
					CostCook walks an owner or manager through the minimum connected kitchen: costing
					defaults, business and supplier details, ingredients, a dish, a menu, and a first
					order.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-4 max-w-[58ch] text-ink-soft">
					Save and return at any time. If the kitchen already has data, the guide shows what
					is complete instead of creating duplicates.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div data-reveal>
				<ol role="list" class="grid gap-x-8 sm:grid-cols-2">
					{
						stages.map((stage, index) => (
							<li class="flex items-center gap-3 border-t border-hairline-strong py-4">
								<span class="flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-green text-sm font-semibold text-white">
									{index + 1}
								</span>
								<span class="font-medium">{stage}</span>
							</li>
						))
					}
				</ol>
				<p class="mt-5 border-t border-hairline-strong pt-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
					Open the calculation at each stage to see how pack price, yield, recipe quantities,
					menu portions, and guest count affect the result.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
